# Vulnerabilities suppressed for the image scan in .github/workflows/docker-images.yml.
#
# One CVE id per line, with a comment saying *why* and when it should be
# revisited. An entry with no expiry is a permanent exception, and there should
# be very few of those: the scan already runs with `ignore-unfixed: true`, so
# anything listed here is something the distribution has fixed and we have
# chosen not to take.
#
# Every image gates on HIGH and CRITICAL -- development images included, since
# the backlog they were assumed to carry turned out to be empty once the
# build-time leftovers were pruned out of ~/.cache/pre-commit. This file is
# therefore the only release valve there is, and the one thing that keeps the
# gate from blocking work on the day a fix lands upstream but not yet in the
# Ubuntu archive. Prefer fixing the image; reach for this when the fix is not
# ours to make, and always with an expiry.
#
# Format (trivy):
#   CVE-2023-12345
#   CVE-2023-12345 exp:2026-01-01
